{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. You're here because of chest pain. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it started a few days ago. At first it only came with walking, but then it lasted longer. Yesterday it went up into my neck and jaw."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Today it didn’t go away with rest. I was sweating, nauseous. It felt different from my last heart attack—no arm numbness this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had stents before, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, one in the LAD artery a while back. I haven’t been taking my meds though—lost them when I was moving around."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. Not taking Plavix or aspirin increases your risk. We’ve started you on aspirin, Plavix, and a heparin drip. We also restarted your metoprolol, lisinopril, and statin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. The pain’s better now, but I’ve been feeling shaky and anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your EKG and blood tests. No signs of a heart attack—troponins are normal. But your echo showed new wall motion issues in the heart, possibly from reduced blood flow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not blocked again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2160-08-06 18:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re concerned a stent might be partially blocked, but since your symptoms improved and tests aren’t showing acute changes, we’ll manage with meds for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2160-08-07 06:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your repeat blood tests are stable. But you mentioned last night you’ve been using heroin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2160-08-07 06:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… I didn’t want to say before. I’ve been using about 2 grams a day. I’m feeling withdrawal—sweating, restless, can’t sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2160-08-07 06:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That explains some symptoms. We’re giving you clonidine and Ativan to help. Social work can help find a detox program."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2160-08-07 06:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I want to get clean. But I don’t want to stay here waiting. I’ll find a bed myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2160-08-07 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. But it’s risky to leave without a plan. Your heart function is reduced—about 40-45% ejection fraction—and stopping meds could lead to another event."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2160-08-07 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I’ll take the meds this time. And I’ll call the detox centers you gave me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re discharging you with a 30-day supply of all your heart meds—Plavix, aspirin, metoprolol, lisinopril, pravastatin. Also, your albuterol inhaler and citalopram."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Aspirin’s 325 mg now? Wasn’t it 81 before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re increasing it temporarily to reduce clotting risk. Go back to 81 mg daily after a few weeks unless your cardiologist says otherwise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I should follow up with my cardiologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, within a week. Also, weigh yourself daily. If you gain more than 3 pounds in a day, call your doctor—it could mean fluid buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll try to stay on track this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you a list of resources for housing and addiction support. Please use them. Your health depends on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We care about your recovery. Take care, and please follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2160-08-07 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to leave. Nurse will give you your prescriptions and instructions."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2160-08-06 18:19:00",
    "admission_end": "2160-08-07 15:26:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a man with a history of coronary artery disease and prior stent placement, was admitted for escalating chest pain radiating to the neck and jaw, accompanied by dyspnea, sweating, and nausea. He had not been taking his cardiac medications, including Plavix and aspirin, for about a month. Initial evaluation showed no acute heart attack, but an echocardiogram revealed new regional wall motion abnormalities, raising concern for possible stent occlusion. His pain resolved with medical therapy. During admission, he disclosed ongoing heroin use and experienced withdrawal symptoms, for which he received clonidine and Ativan. Despite recommendations to remain for detox placement, he chose to self-discharge to seek treatment independently. He was discharged home with a full medication refill, follow-up instructions, and referrals for addiction and housing support.",
    "problems": [
      "Other chest pain",
      "Drug withdrawal",
      "Opioid type dependence, unspecified",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty status",
      "Lack of housing"
    ]
  }
}
